miadi-perms — group read and write on a Miadi host's shared session capture

Several users' agent sessions write into MIADI_SESSIONDATA_ROOT
(/src/_sessiondata by default). miadi-perms.timer runs miadi-perms as root
every 4 hours, which gives the group read and write on every file there that
lacks it.

  systemctl list-timers miadi-perms.timer      when it runs next
  sudo miadi-perms                             run it now (or: sudo miadi-perms <dir>...)
  journalctl -u miadi-perms.service            how many entries each run changed
  sudo systemctl disable --now miadi-perms.timer   stop it; an upgrade keeps it off

Source: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit, packages/miadi/deb
